# Power-on to the lobby server's first screen, over the game's own network stack.
#
#   python3 -I -B tools/rig/rig.py --screen-text --data <dir with save data and a network
#       configuration, see online-netcnf.rig> --eth-net server=<this host's address> \
#       --eth-pcap local/rig-out/a.pcap --script tools/rig/examples/online-lobby.rig
#
# The sign-in step needs the local sign-in patch (not in the repository); without it the
# game stops with a network error when it cannot find Sony's server. The patch must be
# applied before "Internet Game" is chosen. The script ends at the server's terms screen.
# To go on from there (accounts, characters, a game on two machines) start the runner as a
# live session with --interactive-live: docs/issues/live-rig.md section 19, tools/rig/osk.py.
at 300
tapuntil cross 40 g_inFrontend:u8 == 1 timeout 6000
until g_levelName:str8 == intro timeout 3000
wait 320
pnach local/SLUS-20973_4028A55F_signin.pnach *
tap cross 4            # start a new game
wait 90
tap down 4
wait 20
tap cross 4            # the Internet entry: the network menu lists the saved setting
wait 600
tap cross 4            # accept the setting: DHCP, then the gateway and the lobby
wait 900
